;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; FOUR independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the United Kingdom, via Companies House -- and unlike the Delaware
;;     register in the Nasdaq, Inc. catalog (549300L8X1Q78ERXFD06), the register
;;     of record here answers a stable per-entity GET URL, so the register GLEIF
;;     names as both register of record and validation authority (RA000585,
;;     company 05722669) IS cited directly (rows ch-*). :catalog/unreachable is
;;     empty for that reason, not because nothing was tried.
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API (Endava plc is a
;;     foreign private issuer, ticker DAVA on the NYSE, CIK 0001656081)
;;   * the issuer itself, at its own published website www.endava.com -- the
;;     terms page this repository archives (80-data/public/tos.journal.edn
;;     archives https://www.endava.com/terms-and-conditions, the same URL the
;;     issuer-* rows cite)
;;
;; THE ADDRESS IS ONE FACT VISIBLE FROM ALL FOUR AUTHORITIES. GLEIF's legal AND
;; headquarters address, Companies House's registered office, the SEC's business
;; address and the issuer's own printed registered office are all
;; 125 Old Broad Street, London, EC2N 1AR (rows gleif-address, ch-address,
;; sec-street, issuer-registered-office). The Nasdaq catalog needed a paragraph
;; to explain why its two addresses differ; this one needs a sentence to say
;; they do not.
;;
;; THREE HONEST WRINKLES, SO A READER DOES NOT MISREAD THEM AS DRIFT:
;;   1. The issuer's own terms print the company number WITHOUT the leading
;;      zero -- 'Registered in England number: 5722669' -- while GLEIF and
;;      Companies House both print 05722669 (rows gleif-registered-as,
;;      gleif-validated-as, gleif-ocid vs issuer-registered-number). Same
;;      number, two spellings; each row matches its own source's bytes.
;;   2. The SEC submissions record carries "lei":null (row sec-lei-null): the
;;      SEC does NOT corroborate the LEI string itself. The GLEIF<->SEC join in
;;      this catalog rests on legal name + United Kingdom incorporation +
;;      the shared street address + ticker (rows sec-name, sec-state-incorp,
;;      sec-street, sec-ticker), not a shared identifier.
;;   3. GLEIF and Companies House print the legal name upper-case (ENDAVA PLC);
;;      the SEC and the issuer print 'Endava plc'. Case conventions per source,
;;      not four names.
;;
;; ONE STRUCTURAL FACT WORTH READING TWICE: the entity was created 2006-02-27
;; (rows gleif-entity-creation, ch-incorporated -- the two authorities agree to
;; the day), but the LEI was first registered 2014-01-09 (row
;; gleif-initial-registration), while the entity still bore its previous legal
;; name ENDAVA LIMITED (rows gleif-previous-name, ch-previous-name). The LEI is
;; eight years younger than the company it identifies, and today it is managed
;; by EQS Group GmbH, marketing name 'EQS' (rows gleif-managing-lou,
;; gleif-lou-name, gleif-lou-marketing). The catalog cites what GLEIF answers
;; today and claims nothing about earlier managing LOUs.
;;
;; Substrings are taken from the RAW response body and were each checked against
;; the fetched bytes before this file was written (2026-08-22, GLEIF golden copy
;; of 2026-08-21). GLEIF escapes URL slashes in its JSON (gb\/05722669); the
;; ocid row matches that raw escaped form deliberately. Companies House prints
;; the word 'Active' exactly once on the cited page -- the company-status field
;; -- so the body-wide substring match of row ch-status is anchored in fact,
;; and that count was measured, not assumed (2026-08-22).
